nsportation vehicle.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026687671","violation_type_title":"Electronic Child Safety Alarm - used at all times when transporting a child in care (26 TAC §746.5625(c))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5617-a-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215","date":"2025-12-15","original_code":"746.5617(a)(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-02-19","finding":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - List of Children: During a DFPS Investigation, it was determined that a caregiver conducting transportation admitted to not having a list of the children being transported. This resulted in a child in care being left unattended in a vehicle for a period of two hours.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026687636","violation_type_title":"Required Equipment in Vehicles - List of Children (26 TAC §746.5617(a)(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5605-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215","date":"2025-12-15","original_code":"746.5605(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-02-19","finding":"AP Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - No Child Unattended: During a DFPS investigation, it was determined that a child in care was left unattended in a vehicle for two hours.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026692878","violation_type_title":"AP Safety Precautions for Loading and Unloading Children - No Child Unattended (26 TAC §746.5605(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5625-d-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1456771-i20251215","date":"2025-12-15","original_code":"746.5625(d)(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","